## WORKED EXAMPLE

**Question**: "Which suppliers have the highest quality rating?"

**Step 1 — Core concepts**: Primary concept = "quality rating". Secondary = "suppliers". Possible data sources for quality: quality scores, defect rates, inspection results, compliance records, audit outcomes.

**Round A — Explicit**: `Supplier Name` (suppliers), `Quality Score` (quality rating — direct match).

**Round B — Concept-expanding**: `Inspection Result` (description: "quality inspection outcome" — relates to quality ✅), `Defect Count` (description: "number of defects found" — defects are a quality measure ✅), `Compliance Status` (description: "regulatory compliance rating" — compliance relates to quality ✅), `Total Quality Score` (aggregate quality ✅), `Quality Dimension A Score` (breakdown ❌ — Total Quality Score covers it per Rule 11), `Supplier Address` (not quality-related ❌).

**Step 3 — Apply rules**: Final selection: Supplier Name, Quality Score, Inspection Result, Defect Count, Compliance Status, Total Quality Score. Exclude breakdowns and irrelevant columns.

